# --- Secrets: Razorpay + Anthropic credentials must NEVER be committed ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
**/credentials.json

# --- Sealed benchmark ground truth (see docs/PREREGISTRATION.md) ---
# Test-split ground truth is held back until the sealed run is recorded.
bench/test/**/ground_truth.jsonl
bench/test/**/*.sealed

# The DEV corpus is regenerated locally from a seed and is never committed:
# §6.1's split table names the seeds, `assay bench gen` reproduces the files
# from them, and a wildcard `git add` must not be able to sweep a local
# generation into the tree. The directory itself is untouched by this rule --
# it stays exactly where it is, ignored rather than removed.
bench/dev/

# --- Build / runtime ---
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.turbo/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.db
.DS_Store

# --- Run outputs ---
# SCORED RUN ARTIFACTS ARE COMMITTED from spec 1.4.29 (register row
# DATA_MODEL.md §22.2 M48). PROJECT_SPEC.md §7 S10, EVALUATION_SPEC.md §5.5 and
# DECISION_BRIEF.md §C T0-13 each require every claimed number to be traceable
# to a COMMITTED run artifact, while this file excluded runs/ wholesale -- so a
# conforming scored run produced numbers §5.5 forbids reporting.
#
#   runs/<run_id>/<split>/<seed>/<agent>/<llm_mode>/metrics.json   committed
#   runs/report.html                                               committed
#
# The SQLite database stays ignored by *.sqlite above: it is regenerable and is
# not an artifact any reported number is traced to. Scratch output is ignored by
# kind rather than by directory, so a new artifact is committed by default and
# an exclusion has to be argued for.
runs/**/*.log
runs/**/*.tmp
runs/**/tmp/
